# Versioning

VirtFoundry uses **Semantic Versioning 2.0.0** (`1.x.y` since v1.0.0).

## Repositories (release together)

| Repo | Version location | Git tag | Published artifact |
|------|------------------|---------|-------------------|
| [core](https://github.com/virtfoundry/core) | git tag `vX.Y.Z` | `v1.1.0` | GHCR `core`, `ui` |
| [helm-charts](https://github.com/virtfoundry/helm-charts) | `Chart.yaml` `version` + `appVersion` | `v1.1.0` | Helm repo on GitHub Pages |

**Rule:** For a user-facing release, bump **both** repos to the **same** `X.Y.Z` and use the **same** git tag `vX.Y.Z`.

## SemVer

| Bump | When | Examples |
|------|------|----------|
| **PATCH** `1.1.0 → 1.1.1` | Bug fixes, doc-only chart fixes | NAD typo, UI label |
| **MINOR** `1.0.0 → 1.1.0` | New features, chart profile changes | Default VPC, IAM UI |
| **MAJOR** `1.x → 2.0.0` | Breaking API or chart contract | Reserved for major redesign |

Document breaking changes in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Release checklist

1. Update `CHANGELOG.md` in **both** repos
2. Chart: bump `charts/virtfoundry/Chart.yaml` (`version` + `appVersion`)
3. Chart: bump default `images.*` tags in `values.yaml` to match release
4. Merge to `main` (PR + cluster validation when applicable)
5. Tag and push: `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z` in **both** repos
6. CI publishes GHCR images (app) and Helm package (chart)
7. Docs site rebuilds on tag push (MkDocs → GitHub Pages `/docs/`)

## Branch → artifact mapping

- `main` → `latest` images, chart lint CI
- `vX.Y.Z` tag → semver images (`1.1.0`, `1.1`), Helm `index.yaml` entry

Do **not** tag from feature branches except release candidates (`v1.1.0-rc.1` optional).
